  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1136 PM CDT FRI SEP 4 2026\n\nSynoptically, the upper level ridge will oscillate from east to\nwest to east again over the next 7 days. High temperatures are\nforecast to remain in the 95 to 100 degree range during this time\nframe, with afternoon heat indices exceeding 105. Rain chances\nwill edge up over the weekend, as the ridge initially slides\nwestward.\n\nOver the next 24 to 30 hours, rain chances will increase across\nthe southeast after 9 am as a weak boundary moves northward.\nShowers and thunderstorms are expected with high confidence\nbetween 10 am and 3 pm south of I-85. Moving northward, scattered\ndevelopment is anticipated between I-85 and the Livingston to\nAlexander City line from 12 pm to 5 pm, followed by activity from\nTuscaloosa to Sylacauga between 2 pm and 7 pm, and finally from\nJasper to Talladega between 3 pm and 7 pm. Scattered showers and\nstorms are also anticipated north of I-85 throughout the\nafternoon. While isolated activity may precede these windows by\nroughly an hour, the highest probabilities are concentrated\nwithin these periods. Scattered showers will persist through the\nearly evening across central sections. On Sunday, the boundary\nwill shift southward by the afternoon and evening, bringing the\npotential for stronger thunderstorms to the southeast; we will\ncontinue to monitor trends over the next 36 hours.\n\n16",
